\DOC READ_YMM_SSE_TAC

\TYPE {READ_YMM_SSE_TAC : thm -> thm -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Given two component-definition theorems, proves outright a universally
quantified goal equating the reads of two register components over all states.

\DESCRIBE
{SSE_fn : thm} is the defining equation for the first (SSE-style) component,
which appears on the left of the read equation, and {fn : thm} is the defining
equation for the second component, appearing on the right; both equations
define their component in terms of a common underlying component composed with
different sub-component selectors. With {t} and {u} the components defined by
these two theorems:
{
   A ?- !x1. read t x1 = read u x1
   =============================== READ_YMM_SSE_TAC SSE_fn fn
}
\noindent The assumptions are left untouched.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this closing behaviour appears, on goals with no
assumptions whose conclusion is a state-quantified equality between two reads
of components defined from the same underlying component.

\ENDDOC
